      "text": "To solve the problem, we first need to determine the perimeter of the original triangle. The sides of the original triangle are 6 cm, 7 cm, and 9 cm. The perimeter of the original triangle is the sum of its sides:\n\n\\[\n6 + 7 + 9 = 22 \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the perimeter of the similar triangle. The problem states that the perimeter of the similar triangle is 110 cm. Let the scale factor of the similarity be \\( k \\). The perimeter of a similar triangle is given by the original perimeter multiplied by the scale factor \\( k \\). Therefore, we have:\n\n\\[\n22k = 110\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( k \\), we get:\n\n\\[\nk = \\frac{110}{22} = 5\n\\]\n\nThis means that each side of the similar triangle is 5 times the length of the corresponding side of the original triangle. The longest side of the original triangle is 9 cm. Therefore, the longest side of the similar triangle is:\n\n\\[\n9 \\times 5 = 45 \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nThus, the length of the longest side of the similar triangle is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{45}\n\\]",
